# Security headers, applied by Cloudflare Pages to everything it serves.
#
# What these can and cannot do is worth being exact about. They do not hide the
# code: a browser has to receive a script in order to run it, so anyone can read
# the bundle and modify it at runtime in DevTools, and no header changes that.
# What they do is stop the *page* from being turned against its visitor —
# injected scripts, clickjacking frames, content sniffed into the wrong type,
# and the referrer leaking where people came from.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy starts from nothing (`default-src 'none'`) and
# allows, per kind of request, every origin this app is supposed to talk to. Anything else — an injected analytics tag, a script
# smuggled through a dependency, an exfiltration beacon — is refused by the
# browser rather than merely discouraged. Keeping it tight is only possible
# because the app has no third-party scripts at all — and no inline ones, no
# eval and no WebAssembly, so `script-src` is `'self'` and nothing else.
#
# No Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy. `credentialless` was tried and measured:
# the map still worked, but the 3D terrain stopped streaming entirely. What it
# buys — `crossOriginIsolated`, for SharedArrayBuffer and precise timers — is
# nothing this app uses, while the opener policy above already denies other
# windows a handle on this one, and browsers isolate sites by process anyway.
#
# The same headers are applied by `vite preview` (see `vite.config.ts`), so
# a policy that would break the deployed site breaks the local preview first.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; script-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://services.arcgisonline.com https://tiles.maps.eox.at https://s3.amazonaws.com https://t.plnspttrs.net https://cdn.planespotters.net https://api.planespotters.net https://airport-data.com https://*.airport-data.com https://gibs.earthdata.nasa.gov; connect-src 'self' https://services.arcgisonline.com https://tiles.maps.eox.at https://s3.amazonaws.com https://api.adsbdb.com https://api.open-meteo.com https://gibs.earthdata.nasa.gov; font-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; media-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; child-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), fullscreen=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=(), bluetooth=(), midi=(), display-capture=(), xr-spatial-tracking=(), accelerometer=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), encrypted-media=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(self), idle-detection=(), browsing-topics=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains

# Hashed filenames, so these can never go stale.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Natural Earth borders and place names: static, replaced only by a deploy.
/map/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# The manifest, so a home-screen install picks up a new icon within a day.
/site.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Converted airframes: large, and replaced only by a new deploy.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
